---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="How FileLocker Works | Password Protect Files Online" 
  description="Learn how FileLocker secures your files and folders directly in your browser without ever uploading them to a server."
>
  <div class="w-full bg-[#f8fafc] min-h-screen py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <div class="text-center mb-16">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-6 tracking-tight">How FileLocker Works</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-500 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          We believe true privacy means your files should never leave your device. Here is exactly what happens when you protect a file.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-12 shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
        <div class="space-y-12">
          
          <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 items-start">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-16 h-16 bg-blue-50 text-brand-blue rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-2xl font-black">1</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">You select a file or folder</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed">
                When you click "Upload" or drag a file into FileLocker, we do not send it to a server. Instead, your modern web browser simply asks for permission to read the file locally on your hard drive. 
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 items-start">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-16 h-16 bg-blue-50 text-brand-blue rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-2xl font-black">2</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">You create a password</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed">
                We use the password you enter to generate a powerful, mathematical "key" right inside your browser. This key is used to scramble the contents of your file so that it becomes completely unreadable to anyone who doesn't have the password.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 items-start">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-16 h-16 bg-blue-50 text-brand-blue rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-2xl font-black">3</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">We build your Vault</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed">
                FileLocker processes your file chunk-by-chunk and writes the scrambled data into a new <code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded text-sm text-brand-blue">.vault</code> file. Because this happens directly on your device, it is incredibly fast and there are no artificial file size limits.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 items-start">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-16 h-16 bg-green-50 text-green-600 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-2xl font-black">
              <svg class="w-8 h-8" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">You save the result</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed">
                Your browser will prompt you to save the resulting protected file. You can now safely email it, upload it to cloud storage, or put it on a USB drive knowing it is mathematically impossible to open without your password.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 text-center">
        <a href="/lock-file" class="bg-brand-blue hover:bg-brand-blue-dark text-white font-bold py-4 px-10 rounded-full shadow-lg transition-transform hover:scale-105 active:scale-95 inline-block text-lg">
          Protect a File Now
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
